            "text": "{\"decision\":\"request_changes\",\"thresholds_preserved\":false,\"contradiction_requires_evidence\":true,\"controls_consistent\":true,\"reason\":\"The design states the intended thresholds and provides strong safeguards against label leakage, retrospective regrading, and overstated validation claims. However, the prospective aggregation does not explicitly make required-disclosure completeness or the derived missingness result a pass condition, and it does not explicitly retain the no-unsupported-guidance threshold. As written, it is unclear whether a report could pass despite failing one of those stated requirements.\",\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"medium\",\"issue\":\"The plan preserves all required disclosures and no unsupported guidance, but the validation aggregation lists support and coverage thresholds, critical-claim checks, and a derived missingness value without explicitly requiring required_disclosures_complete=true, missingness_correct=true, or no unsupported guidance for a report to pass. A noncritical omitted disclosure could therefore appear to pass the listed numeric gates.\",\"action\":\"Specify these as explicit report-level pass conditions in the deterministic aggregation, including that missingness_correct must be true, and define how unsupported guidance is identified and fails a report. Add boundary tests showing that a noncritical omitted required disclosure and unsupported guidance cannot pass.\"}] }",
