    "reason": "The design states the intended thresholds and provides strong safeguards against label leakage, retrospective regrading, and overstated validation claims. However, the prospective aggregation does not explicitly make required-disclosure completeness or the derived missingness result a pass condition, and it does not explicitly retain the no-unsupported-guidance threshold. As written, it is unclear whether a report could pass despite failing one of those stated requirements.",
    "findings": [
